      "writtenOn": "2017-07-28T16:40:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Attempting to understand why you decided to abstract away the cache. The original thought was the cache would be used regardless if the data came from the the config or from a remote call. This way the same code path was exercised regardless of the source of the data.\n\nWould you please explain why you decided to abstract the cache in this way? Also, if we are to abstract the cache we need to put it in a separate source file.",
      "revId": "203629cf4a97c9d41025101510b7a9107699298d",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a1a2d67_8d8fb523",
        "filename": "src/main/java/org/opencord/sadis/SubscriberAndDeviceInformationAdapter.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000097
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-31T04:32:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that the cache is required only when the amount of data is huge and we don\u0027t want all the instances to have a copy. When the data comes from ONOS configuration, each of the instances already has a copy, so there isn\u0027t a reason to cache it.\n\nYes I agree that it might be better to have the cache feed of the ONOS configuration also, but only from a testing perspective, so that the same code path is tested for external or internal data source.\n\nLet me know your thoughts, I can change if you still want the cache to be used irrespective of the data source.",
      "parentUuid": "1a1a2d67_e2699826",
      "revId": "203629cf4a97c9d41025101510b7a9107699298d",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
